# dotenvx + Bitwarden (local env)

Canonical how-to: [`docs/dotenvx.md`](docs/dotenvx.md). Stack: [dotenvx](https://dotenvx.com/) · [Bitwarden custody](https://dotenvx.com/docs/custody/bitwarden/) · Resilio Sync.

## Model

| Place | Format | Private key |
|---|---|---|
| Dev PC (Win/macOS) project `.env` | Encrypted (`encrypted:…`) | Bitwarden / local `.env.keys` — not git, not Dropbox |
| **Resilio SoR** | Encrypted `.env` only | Never |
| VPS `/opt/twitch-telegram-bot` | **Plaintext** `.env` (compose / deploy) | N/A |
| Public git | `.env.example` only | Never `.env.keys` / `DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY` / `BW_SESSION` |

### Encrypted `.env` sync (Resilio / Dropbox)

Source of truth for the **encrypted** file between personal machines:

| Machine | Path (this Mac) | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Ekaterinas-MacBook-Air | `/Users/Blogger/Dropbox/.env` | Resilio folder named Dropbox (`~/Dropbox`) |

- Sync is **Resilio**, not Dropbox Inc. cloud. Folder may still be named `Dropbox`.
- **Always** take the current encrypted `.env` from that Resilio path into the project (copy over repo `.env`).
- After `dotenvx set` / encrypt / rotate on any PC: write the new encrypted `.env` **back** to the Resilio path.
- Never put `.env.keys` or plaintext secrets in the Resilio folder.
- Do **not** commit production ciphertext to the public GitHub remote.

**If the Resilio/Dropbox path is missing** (other machine, different folder name, not mounted): **stop and ask the user** for the local path. Do not invent `~/Dropbox`, OneDrive, or CasaOS paths.

## Agent must

- Load via `dotenv_loader` / `config.py` — never invent a second parser
- Prefer `dotenvx set KEY "value"` for encrypted local updates (then sync VPS plaintext per [`twitch-client-secret.mdc`](twitch-client-secret.mdc) **and** copy encrypted `.env` to the Resilio path)
- Before trusting local repo `.env`, refresh from Resilio SoR when that path exists
- Run local bot with `dotenvx run -- python main.py` (or after Bitwarden unlock / `.env.keys`)
- Keep `.env.keys`, plaintext secrets, Hostkey/API keys, `BW_SESSION` out of chat, commits, logs — print counts/prefixes only
- Refuse committing `.env.keys`; remind `dotenvx bitwarden up` if a private key appears on disk after encrypt/rotate
- Know that `dotenvx bitwarden pull` needs a **local custody reference** from a prior `bitwarden up` on this machine; otherwise materialize `.env.keys` via `bw get password <item-id>` (never print the key)
- Docker image: no `.env` / `.env.keys` (`.dockerignore`)

## Agent must not

- Put private key or vault session in source / README / rules examples with real values
- Put `.env.keys` into Resilio/Dropbox
- Replace VPS plaintext workflow with encrypted-only without an explicit user request
- Log decrypted env or `bw` / Hostkey tokens
- Assume Bitwarden custody is done while `.env.keys` still holds `DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY=…`
- Guess the sync folder on an unknown machine — ask

## Quick commands

```bash
# refresh ciphertext from Resilio SoR (this Mac)
cp -f ~/Dropbox/.env .env

dotenvx set SOME_KEY "new-value"
cp -f .env ~/Dropbox/.env   # publish back to Resilio

export BW_SESSION="$(bw unlock --raw)"
dotenvx bitwarden up        # custody after encrypt/rotate (removes .env.keys)
dotenvx run -- python main.py
```

PowerShell may block `.ps1` — use the commands above or `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\env-run.ps1`.
